examples.question_text:
a) A circle has circumference $C$, diameter $d$ and radius $r$. Write the calculation that gives $\pi$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw[thick] (0,0) circle (1.7);
\draw[thick] (-1.7,0)--(1.7,0);
\fill (0,0) circle (1.5pt);
\path (0,-0.35) node {$d$};
\draw[thick] (0,0)--(60:1.7);
\path (0.65,0.65) node {$r$};
\path (0,2.05) node {Circumference $C$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
b) About how many lengths equal to the diameter fit around its circumference? Explain why using the radius gives a different number.
c) Write $\pi$ correct to $3$ decimal places and to $4$ decimal places.
